 5. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Touchdown in Taiwan. Photo: Wang Jinfu/Taiwan Military News Agency

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🇹🇼 The first batch of Lockheed Martin F-16 Block 70s arrived in Taiwan, the island's military announced. The new-build jets landed near Taitung, a city on the southeastern side of the island .

 Why it matters: This is just the beginning. Additional aircraft are expected soon, according to Defense Minister Wellington Koo. 💭 My thought bubble: This is good news for Taiwan — especially as 2027 nears. 🚀 The U.S. Army selected Anduril Industries, Castelion, Lockheed Martin, Mach Industries and RTX to prototype the Precision Strike Missile Increment 4. Fly-offs are planned.

 Why it matters: The missiles are expected to be able to hit moving land and sea targets at ranges greater than 620 miles. 💭 My thought bubble: That's roughly doubling PrSM's range, as Inside Defense pointed out. 📈 Northrop Grumman's self-funded YFQ-48A flew autonomously for the first time, executing taxi, takeoff, in-flight maneuvers and landing in Mojave, California .

 Why it matters: "Talon Blue's first flight is one step toward a new generation of autonomous capabilities," Northrop's Craig Woolston said in a statement. "Every flight and lesson strengthens our broader autonomy work and sharpens what comes next." 💭 My thought bubble: I was one of a lucky few who attended the Talon unveiling in December. More on that here . 
 
